XAScraft
========

XAScraft is a web application built on xraylarch (Larch), the X-ray absorption and
fluorescence analysis library by Matthew Newville and the xraylarch contributors:
https://github.com/xraypy/xraylarch. Larch is not included in this repository; it is
installed from the upstream commit pinned in larch-patches/PIN.

The following parts of this repository come from xraylarch and are distributed under
its MIT license (see LICENSE):

- examples/: the example data and scripts, taken unchanged from xraylarch at commit
  8d6cd41c2b2a19260dbc80519c3c95211331d4fc, except the files the XAScraft team added
  after that commit:
    examples/athena/curated_demo/  (the whole folder; data sources are recorded in its
                                    manifest.json and README.md)
    examples/xafsdata/Cu2O_standard.0001

- larch-patches/series/: changes to xraylarch source files, made by the XAScraft team on
  top of the pinned upstream commit. Each patch modifies files that come from xraylarch.
